= The Leak

Thousands of internal party e-mails appear on a transparency website. U.S. intelligence agencies will later attribute the hack to Russian military intelligence. The e-mails show staffers disparaging the insurgent campaign. The convention opens in disarray.

- @apologize: Apologize, replace the chair, and move on.
- @blame: Focus on the foreign interference.
- @security: Rebuild cybersecurity quickly.

@apologize
subtitle: Costs the party some pride.
on-arrival: unity += 3; prog_dissent -= 4; media_trust += 1; stability += 1

The chair steps down. The convention proceeds. The story will not go away.

@blame
subtitle: Right on facts, mixed politically.
on-arrival: stability += 3; media_trust += 1; prog_dissent += 3; enthusiasm -= 1

We say, accurately, that a foreign government is trying to influence our election. Some hear it as an excuse.

@security
subtitle: Boring, necessary.
on-arrival: funds -= 2 if funds >= 2; stability += 3; media_trust += 1

The party hires real security professionals. Too late for this cycle, in time for the next.
